  "raw_text": "No. “Current branch” is time-dependent: the branch may have advanced, been rebased, or now point to a different commit. Sharing a repository does not bind the note to the currently checked-out revision.\n\nYou need a stable identifier—ideally the tested commit SHA—plus the test command/environment and results. Without that, the note only shows that some unspecified revision of the branch passed at the time it was written.",
